#Problem APEX 4.1.11

## DBsubject(Calculus - single variable)
## DBchapter(Applications of differentiation)
## DBsection(Newton's method)
## Institution(Valdosta State University)
## Author(S. V. Ault)
## MLT(Newton-f-value-graph)
## Level(3)
## MO(1)
## TitleText1('APEX Calculus')
## AuthorText1('Hartman')
## EditionText1('3.0')
## Section1('4.1')
## Problem1('11')

DOCUMENT();

# Load whatever macros you need for the problem
loadMacros('PGstandard.pl', 'PGML.pl', 'PGlateximage.pl', 'PGcourse.pl');

$a = random(-0.10, 0.075, 0.005);
$f    = Formula("x^2 * cos(x) + (x-1)*sin(x) + $a")->reduce;
$df   = $f->D('x');

### Root Finding ###
$a[0] = Real(-2);
$a[1] = Real($a[0] - $f->eval(x => $a[0]) / $df->eval(x => $a[0]));
while ($a[-2] != $a[-1] || $#a < 5) {
        push @a, Real($a[-1] - $f->eval(x => $a[-1]) / $df->eval(x => $a[-1]));
}

$b[0] = Real(0);
$b[1] = Real($b[0] - $f->eval(x => $b[0]) / $df->eval(x => $b[0]));
while ($b[-2] != $b[-1] || $#b < 5) {
        push @b, Real($b[-1] - $f->eval(x => $b[-1]) / $df->eval(x => $b[-1]));
}

$c[0] = Real(0.5);
$c[1] = Real($c[0] - $f->eval(x => $c[0]) / $df->eval(x => $c[0]));
while ($c[-2] != $c[-1] || $#c < 5) {
        push @c, Real($c[-1] - $f->eval(x => $c[-1]) / $df->eval(x => $c[-1]));
}

$d[0] = Real(2);
$d[1] = Real($d[0] - $f->eval(x => $d[0]) / $df->eval(x => $d[0]));
while ($d[-2] != $d[-1] || $#d < 5) {
        push @d, Real($d[-1] - $f->eval(x => $d[-1]) / $df->eval(x => $d[-1]));
}

Context()->flags->set(
    tolerance => 0.0001,
    tolType   => "absolute",
);

$ans = List("$a[-1], $b[-1], $c[-1], $d[-1]");

$graph = createLaTeXImage();
$graph->texPackages(['pgfplots']);
$graph->BEGIN_LATEX_IMAGE
\begin{tikzpicture}
        \begin{axis}[
                        xmin=-3,
                        xmax=3,
                        ymin=-3,
                        ymax=3,
                        axis lines=middle,
                        minor xtick={-3,...,3},
                        minor ytick={0},
                        grid=both
                ]
                \addplot[domain=-6:3, thick, smooth]{x^2 * cos(deg(x)) + (x-1)*sin(deg(x)) + $a};
        \end{axis}
\end{tikzpicture}
END_LATEX_IMAGE

$altText =
    "A graph that starts in the 3rd quadrant, rises through a intercept near "
    . "x=-2$, reaches a maximum, dips through a x-intercept around x=0, hits a minimum "
    . "near x=0.25, crosses the x-axis to a maximum about x=1, then falls through an "
    . "intercept near x=2";

BEGIN_PGML
Use Newton's Method to approximate all roots of the given
function, within the given interval,
accurate to 4 places after the decimal.  Use
the graph below to obtain good initial approximations.
[```  
   f(x) = [$f], \quad \text{on } (-3, 3)
```]

>> [![$altText]!]{$graph}{400} <<

Root(s): [_]{$ans}{30}

(Separate multiple answers by commas.)
END_PGML

###################################

BEGIN_PGML_SOLUTION
Set up the iterative formula for Newton's Method:
[```
    \begin{aligned}
    x_{n+1} 
    & = x_n - \frac{f(x_n)}{f'(x_n)} \\
    & = x_n - \frac{x_n^2\cos x_n + (x_n - 1)\sin x_n}{-x_n^2\sin x_n + 2x_n\cos x_n + (x_n-1)\cos x_n + \sin x_n}
    \end{aligned}
```]

There are four roots.  The smallest is near [`x = [$xa0]`]. Using Newton's Method,
[```
  \begin{aligned}
    x_0 &= [$a[0]] \\
    x_1 &\approx [$a[1]] \\
    x_2 &\approx [$a[2]] \\
    x_3 &\approx [$a[3]] \\
    x_4 &\approx [$a[4]] \\
    & \vdots
  \end{aligned}
```]

The next root is near [`x = [$b[0]]`].
Using Newton's Method,
[```
  \begin{aligned}
    x_0 &= [$b[0]] \\
    x_1 &\approx [$b[1]] \\
    x_2 &\approx [$b[2]] \\
    x_3 &\approx [$b[3]] \\
    x_4 &\approx [$b[4]] \\
    & \vdots
  \end{aligned}
```]

The largest root is near [`x = [$c[0]]`].
Using Newton's Method,
[```
  \begin{aligned}
    x_0 &= [$c[0]] \\
    x_1 &\approx [$c[1]] \\
    x_2 &\approx [$c[2]] \\
    x_3 &\approx [$c[3]] \\
    x_4 &\approx [$c[4]] \\
    & \vdots
  \end{aligned}
```]

The largest root is near [`x = [$d[0]]`].
Using Newton's Method,
[```
  \begin{aligned}
    x_0 &= [$d[0]] \\
    x_1 &\approx [$d[1]] \\
    x_2 &\approx [$d[2]] \\
    x_3 &\approx [$d[3]] \\
    x_4 &\approx [$d[4]] \\
    & \vdots
  \end{aligned}
```]

END_PGML_SOLUTION
ENDDOCUMENT();

